// OsImportSlot — the OS primitives a dynamically-linked target reaches through an import
// table, and the slot index a call site records for its writer to patch.
//
// ⭐ THE SLOT-INDEX MODEL IS OS-NEUTRAL; ONLY THE SYMBOL SPELLING IS NOT. A call site emits
// "call through import slot k" and the object writer resolves k to an address: the Mach-O
// writer against a `__got` entry dyld binds, the PE writer against an IAT entry (`IatSlot`,
// the identical shape). Nothing about `k` is Mach-O, which is why this enum does NOT belong
// in `Targets/Macos/` — two files under `Targets/Arm64/` (the isel and the entry stub) named
// a Mach-O type to say "the exit primitive", a layering leak that only became visible when
// arm64-linux arrived and needed the same three primitives with NO import table at all.
//
// The per-format SYMBOL map stays with its writer (`machoImportSymbol` renders the Mach-O
// ABI's leading underscore: a C `exit` is the symbol `_exit`), because that IS format
// knowledge. Adding an import is still: append a case here and its symbol there.
//
// ⚠ arm64-LINUX USES NONE OF THIS. Linux permits raw syscalls, so `osExit`/`osWriteStdout`/
// `osAllocPages` lower to `svc #0` and the ELF image carries no import table, no GOT and no
// dynamic linker (see `Arm64Runtime.arm64OsCallKind`). The enum is reached only on the
// import-table route.
//
// `exit` terminates the process with main's return code. `write` is both the panic runtime's
// route to stderr and the `osWriteStdout`/`print` primitive. `mmap` is the page source
// `osAllocPages` bottoms out in; MAP_ANON returns ZEROED pages, satisfying the slab's zeroing
// contract. No `munmap`: the slab never decommits, so a page-free import would be dead.
export enum OsImportSlot
	exit
	write
	mmap
end 'OsImportSlot'

// The import slot index a call site records and the writer patches against. One accessor
// over the enum, exactly like `iatSlotIndex`.
export function osImportSlotIndex(slot OsImportSlot) returns RelocSlotIndex
	return slot.ordinal as RelocSlotIndex
end 'osImportSlotIndex'
